# JEX Assessment — API manual verification
# Run the API using the HTTPS launch profile.
# Base URL from Properties/launchSettings.json.
#
# IMPORTANT: This walkthrough assumes a FRESH database after applying migrations.
# Run the requests in order, one at a time. On a fresh database, the four
# companies receive IDs 1–4 and the four backoffice vacancies receive IDs 1–4.
# If you already have data, replace these example IDs with IDs from responses,
# or start with a new database and apply the existing migration.
#
# In Visual Studio Package Manager Console (after creating a fresh database):
#   Update-Database
#
# Separate each request with ### and a blank line after Content-Type.

@host = https://localhost:7221


# ============================================================
# USER STORY 1 — BACKOFFICE: COMPANIES
# ============================================================

### 01 — Create JEX (expected: 201 Created; ID 1 on fresh database)
POST {{host}}/api/companies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "JEX",
  "address": "Rotterdam"
}

### 02 — Create Microsoft (expected: 201 Created; ID 2)
POST {{host}}/api/companies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Microsoft",
  "address": "Amsterdam"
}

### 03 — Create Contoso (expected: 201 Created; ID 3)
POST {{host}}/api/companies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Contoso",
  "address": "Silicon Valley"
}

### 04 — Create a company without vacancies (expected: 201 Created; ID 4)
POST {{host}}/api/companies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Example Company",
  "address": "Utrecht"
}

### 05 — Get all companies (expected: 200 OK; four companies)
GET {{host}}/api/companies

### 06 — Get JEX by ID (expected: 200 OK)
GET {{host}}/api/companies/1

### 07 — Update JEX (expected: 204 No Content)
PUT {{host}}/api/companies/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "JEX Nederland",
  "address": "Rotterdam"
}

### 08 — Verify updated company (expected: 200 OK)
GET {{host}}/api/companies/1


# ============================================================
# USER STORY 1 — BACKOFFICE: VACANCIES
# ============================================================

### 09 — Create active JEX vacancy (expected: 201 Created; vacancy ID 1)
POST {{host}}/api/vacancies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "companyId": 1,
  "title": "Senior .NET Developer",
  "description": "Develop and maintain backend APIs",
  "isActive": true
}

### 10 — Create inactive JEX vacancy (expected: 201 Created; vacancy ID 2)
POST {{host}}/api/vacancies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "companyId": 1,
  "title": "Junior .NET Developer",
  "description": "Support the backend development team",
  "isActive": false
}

### 11 — Create active Microsoft vacancy (expected: 201 Created; vacancy ID 3)
POST {{host}}/api/vacancies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "companyId": 2,
  "title": "Azure Developer",
  "description": "Develop cloud applications on Azure",
  "isActive": true
}

### 12 — Create inactive Contoso vacancy (expected: 201 Created; vacancy ID 4)
POST {{host}}/api/vacancies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "companyId": 3,
  "title": "Java Developer",
  "description": "Develop Java applications",
  "isActive": false
}

### 13 — Get all vacancies (expected: 200 OK; four vacancies)
GET {{host}}/api/vacancies

### 14 — Get JEX vacancy by ID (expected: 200 OK)
GET {{host}}/api/vacancies/1

### 15 — Update JEX vacancy (expected: 204 No Content)
PUT {{host}}/api/vacancies/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "companyId": 1,
  "title": "Senior Backend Developer",
  "description": "Build scalable REST APIs",
  "isActive": true
}

### 16 — Verify updated vacancy (expected: 200 OK)
GET {{host}}/api/vacancies/1


# ============================================================
# USER STORY 2 — COMPANIES WITH ACTIVE VACANCIES
# ============================================================

### 17 — Active vacancy listing (expected: 200 OK)
# Expected: JEX and Microsoft only, each with its active vacancy.
# Excluded: Contoso (only inactive vacancy), Example Company (no vacancies).
# JEX's inactive Junior .NET Developer vacancy must not be included.
GET {{host}}/api/companies/with-active-vacancies


# ============================================================
# USER STORY 3 — PUBLIC VACANCY CREATION
# ============================================================

### 18 — Public creation, title only (expected: 201 Created; isActive false)
POST {{host}}/api/companies/1/vacancies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Full Stack .NET Developer"
}

### 19 — Public creation, title and optional description (expected: 201 Created; isActive false)
POST {{host}}/api/companies/2/vacancies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Azure Backend Developer",
  "description": "Develop cloud-native applications"
}

### 20 — Verify public vacancies are not in active listing (expected: 200 OK)
# Only the original active vacancies should appear for JEX and Microsoft.
GET {{host}}/api/companies/with-active-vacancies


# ============================================================
# VALIDATION AND ERROR RESPONSES
# ============================================================

### 21 — Missing public vacancy title (expected: 400 Bad Request)
POST {{host}}/api/companies/1/vacancies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Missing mandatory title"
}

### 22 — Whitespace-only public vacancy title (expected: 400 Bad Request)
POST {{host}}/api/companies/1/vacancies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "   "
}

### 23 — Public vacancy for nonexistent company (expected: 404 Not Found)
POST {{host}}/api/companies/999999/vacancies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Senior .NET Developer"
}

### 24 — Backoffice vacancy for nonexistent company (expected: 404 Not Found)
POST {{host}}/api/vacancies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "companyId": 999999,
  "title": "Backend Developer",
  "description": "Develop APIs",
  "isActive": true
}

### 25 — Missing company name (expected: 400 Bad Request)
POST {{host}}/api/companies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "address": "Rotterdam"
}

### 26 — Nonexistent vacancy (expected: 404 Not Found)
GET {{host}}/api/vacancies/999999


# ============================================================
# DELETE SCENARIOS — RUN THESE LAST
# ============================================================

### 27 — Delete company with vacancies (expected: 409 Conflict)
DELETE {{host}}/api/companies/1

### 28 — Delete inactive Contoso vacancy (expected: 204 No Content)
DELETE {{host}}/api/vacancies/4

### 29 — Delete Contoso after removing its only vacancy (expected: 204 No Content)
DELETE {{host}}/api/companies/3

### 30 — Delete company without vacancies (expected: 204 No Content)
DELETE {{host}}/api/companies/4

### 31 — Verify deleted company is gone (expected: 404 Not Found)
GET {{host}}/api/companies/4
